## Session 19 summary

**State of the gate:** 17/19 criteria green in `.criteria_results.json`; the blockers are `scaling_curve --nodes 16` and the perf criteria, plus the final end-to-end `verify_ship.sh` run.

**Root causes found this session (RULE 4, stack-sampled):**

1. **`mxfs_drevalidate` did a synchronous SCSI FUA read per cached directory lookup** (sess86 GENMISS check) — 32/43 stack samples. Solo rsync with one *idle* peer mounted: 127s vs ~5s truly-single-node. **Fixed** with a DLM hold-epoch fast path: new `i_dlm_epoch` in xfs_inode (init=1, bumped at all six `i_dlm_mode→NL` sites in xfs_mxfs_dlm.c), stamped into `dentry->d_time` after coordinated validation; cached lookups with grant held + epoch match return valid with zero I/O (positive and negative dentries). Verified: FUA reads vanished from the profile, 127s → 62s.

2. **`mxfs_dlm_dir_durable_signal` ran `xfs_log_force(SYNC)` + dir-block bwrite per create/remove/rename** (~7ms × 8714 files ≈ the remaining 62s; 12-13/21 samples). First fix attempt (coalesced 20ms delayed worker, build `499446C3`) **caused dir3 verifier shutdowns in <1s** — the async flush races the lockless FUA oracles that assume committed ⇒ on-platter. Reverted the worker entirely; `durable_signal` is now **publish-only** (ring staging, no disk I/O), on the argument that peer reads always coordinate through the DLM and our BAST release drain (invariant #1) makes blocks durable before any peer can read them.

**Work remaining (next session, in order):**
1. **Not yet done:** gate the three lockless FUA oracles in `mxfs_drevalidate` (GENMISS / RESURRECT / TYPEMISS, pal/linux/xfs_super.c) on `READ_ONCE(ip->i_dlm_mode) == MXFS_LOCK_NL` — with publish-only dirsig the platter lags until AIL push, and on a re-mkfs'd LUN those oracles read *previous-incarnation* dinodes (valid old gens) and falsely mark fresh dirs stale (the DIRMISS/`names=[]` clobber chain observed). Without this gate the publish-only build will likely corrupt again.
2. Bump VERSION (still 0.5.1), `make modules`, deploy, re-run `scripts/diag_2node_rsync.sh` — target solo ≈ 5-10s, phase B concurrent without shutdown.
3. Also still open: the **`xfs_trans_cancel` dirty-cancel shutdown in `xfs_rename`** seen on the *old* build (CB1C5FEF) under 2-node concurrent rsync — pre-existing, must be re-checked once perf fixes are in.
4. Then the criteria battery (cache_coherency, strong_consistency, zero_silent_loss, crash_consistency, single_node_paired at 126-167% needs re-measuring, rsync_paired, scaling_curve 330s budget, posix_semantics 16) and the single end-to-end `verify_ship.sh`.

Criteria marker **not** written — gate is not green.

